# {{project_name}}

Rust / Axum / SQLx / SQLite API generated by Miblo.

Run `cargo run`, or open this project in `miblo` and press `r`.
SQLite creates `miblo.sqlite` automatically. Migrations run at startup.
No database server or SQLx CLI is needed. `.env` is already configured.
Keep `.env` and SQLite database files out of Git.

In Miblo, press `a` to add a model: it creates a Rust model, SQL migration,
and GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE routes. Press `b` for database actions and migrations.
Existing resource code is preserved when adding another model.

List queries support limit/offset. Private fields are omitted from responses;
private does not mean encrypted or hashed. Authentication is not included.
Use handwritten migrations for changes to existing tables. Switching database
engines for an existing project requires an explicit migration of code and data.

Run `cargo test` to check the generated project.

## Database relations

Miblo creates each table's integer primary key `id` automatically. While adding a
new model, choose a relation to another model: it generates an integer foreign
key, its index and SQL constraint. The database enforces missing-parent checks
and the selected RESTRICT, CASCADE or SET NULL deletion rule; SET NULL requires
an optional field. CRUD requests accept the foreign-key ID, without nested joins.
Create the parent row first, then supply its ID when creating a linked row.

Use `miblo` then `d` to inspect actual tables, PK/FK columns and links; `p` shows
the declared model definitions. Apply pending migrations with `b`. Existing
models' keys are not rewritten by adding a new model.
